     "text": "{\"cost\": 8, \"rationale\": \"Shortest path, with no defences deployed: (1) phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. (2) pivot_internal gives reach_internal; it is allowed because the network is not segmented. (3) auth_ciserver gives foothold_ciserver. (4) escalate_ciserver gives admin_ciserver; it is allowed because the CI server is not patched. (5) leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin. (6) auth_db gives foothold_db. (7) escalate_db gives admin_db. (8) exfiltrate_db gives exfiltrated. No step can be dropped. Every exfiltration technique needs a foothold, an admin escalation and then the exfiltrate step, which is 3 techniques, and all of these need stolen_dbadmin and reach_internal. The cheapest source of stolen_dbadmin is the CI server chain (auth, escalate, leak), which is 3 techniques and needs stolen_user plus reach_internal. Phishing supplies both a foothold and stolen_user in one step, and pivot_internal adds one more. The DC and ADFS routes are longer because they also need stolen_admin through kerberoasting and then auth, escalate and dump steps.\"}"
